// Test: bugfixes/validator_field_rejects_value
// Grammar: function_call (validator.field)
// Semantic: FUNC002 — `validator.field(v, name)` takes two arguments; rules
//   never hold data, so a value argument is rejected with a hint to pass the
//   data to `validator.run` / `validator.runField`
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.184
// Expected output:
// Expected error:
//   error[FUNC002]
//   validator.field(v, name) takes no value
//
// Regression: the compiler accepted `validator.field(v, name, value)` and
// stored the value in the field rule.

start:
	integer v = validator.field(validator.create(), "email", "ada@example.com")
	print(validator.isOk(validator.run(v, 0)))
